      "texts": [
        "## Primary Request and Intent\n- Sequence of acceptance-test instructions from the user, each bounded and explicit:\n  - \"Call baseline_receipt exactly once, then report the exact receipt it returns. Do not infer it or call other tools.\"\n  - \"A new tool late_receipt is now available. Call late_receipt exactly once and report its exact returned receipt.\"\n  - \"The baseline tool has been withdrawn. Using only the currently available tool late_receipt, read its receipt once more and quote it. Do not call baseline_receipt.\"\n  - \"Continue after plugin reload: call late_receipt once and report its exact receipt. No other tool is needed.\"\n  - \"Please apply /receipt to this reply.\" \u2192 then \"Use the receipt skill for this turn. Load its current instructions with the skill tool first, then follow them. Do not rely on the earlier loaded copy.\"\n  - \"The installed Skill catalog has changed. Load the currently offered replacement receipt skill using the skill tool, then follow its current instructions. Do not load the removed receipt skill.\"\n  - \"Use read_image to inspect /tmp/ds41f-alpha2-e2e/workspace/image-A.png. Describe its shape, color, and printed identifier briefly. Remember this observation for a later comparison.\"\n  - \"Now use read_image on /tmp/ds41f-alpha2-e2e/workspace/image-B.png. Briefly report its shape, color, and printed identifier, then compare it with your earlier A observation.\"\n\n## Key Technical Concepts\n- Tool-call discipline: exactly-once invocation, no tool substitution, no inferred outputs.\n- Skill catalog hot-reload: skills removed/replaced mid-session; only names in the latest catalog are valid.\n- Skill tool loading (`skill`) with exact skill name; skill instructions must be followed, resource paths relative to skill base directory.\n- Image inspection via `read_image` (normalized read-only copies returned under `/tmp/ds41f-alpha2-e2e/home/attachments/v1/objects/...`).\n\n## Files and Code\n- `/tmp/ds41f-alpha2-e2e/workspace/image-A.png`: 544x544 PNG, sha256 `3c56ebabdb297c9ee4bf451a9cb698e40ea3f7ef88f46731e1ca4f3344cdb90a`; upward-pointing solid blue triangle on white with black identifier `AX-31`.\n- `/tmp/ds41f-alpha2-e2e/workspace/image-B.png`: 544x544 PNG, sha256 `5f0f9d985f5620604e6aef01214629d300ea3b8bdbc275bf3be5e2855c1bd6dd`; solid orange square on white with black identifier `BX-72`.\n- Skill base dirs: `/tmp/ds41f-alpha2-e2e/home/skills/receipt` (removed skill `receipt`), `/tmp/ds41f-alpha2-e2e/home/skills/receipt-next` (current skill `receipt-next`).\n\n## Errors and Fixes\n- (none)\n\n## Pending Jobs\n- Report shape/color/identifier for image-B and compare with the A observation (requested, not yet delivered).\n\n## Current Work\n- `read_image` on image-B completed: orange square, identifier `BX-72`. Comparison with A (blue triangle, `AX-31`) still owed in the reply.\n\n## Next Step\n- Reply briefly: B is an orange square labeled `BX-72`; A was a blue triangle labeled `AX-31` \u2014 differing in shape (square vs triangle), color (orange vs blue), and identifier.\n\n## Critical Context\n- Receipt values observed (exact): baseline = `BOOT-438`; `late_receipt` = `LATE-927` (returned consistently on all three calls, including after plugin reload).\n- `baseline_receipt` is withdrawn; must never be called again.\n- Skill outputs to state verbatim: old `receipt` skill \u2192 `SKILL-ALPHA-614`; replacement `receipt-next` skill \u2192 `SKILL-BETA-827`.\n- Bounded-instruction style: each turn only the named tool, exactly once, no extra tools, exact quotes only \u2014 never claim an effect without executing it."
